/**
 * Pre-norm residual cross-attention sub-layer of a transformer block — the pre-normalization, the
 * cross-attention over an encoder context, and the residual connection around both of them.
 *
 * This file replaces the Java assembly that used to live in
 * TransformerBlockFeatures.transformerBlock(...), which built this sub-layer as a SequentialBlock
 * (the cross-attention pre-normalization, then the cross-attention) wrapped in residual():
 *   SequentialBlock crossAttentionWithNorm = new SequentialBlock(blockShape);
 *   crossAttentionWithNorm.add(norm(normType, crossAttPreNormWeight, crossAttPreNormBias));
 *   crossAttentionWithNorm.add(sequenceCrossAttention(...));
 *   block.add(residual(crossAttentionWithNorm));
 * transformerBlock now binds the normalization weights, builds the cross-attention block, and loads
 * the layer of the normalization family it is asked for
 * (TransformerBlockFeatures.crossAttentionResidualSublayer), so there is one definition of the
 * sub-layer structure and it is here. It is the cross-attention sibling of
 * self_attention_sublayer.pdsl and feed_forward_sublayer.pdsl, and reads as the same diagram: norm,
 * body, residual.
 *
 * There is one layer per normalization family (LayerNorm or RMSNorm):
 *
 *   cross_attention_sublayer_layernorm   LayerNorm
 *   cross_attention_sublayer_rmsnorm     RMSNorm
 *
 * Unlike the self-attention and feed-forward sub-layers, the cross-attention sub-layer is never
 * adaptive-layernorm (adaLN-Zero) modulated: a diffusion transformer conditions its self-attention
 * and feed-forward on the global vector, but attends to the encoder context unconditionally
 * (x = x + cross_attention(norm(x))). So there is no modulate stage, no output gate, and no
 * _modulated variant.
 *
 * The cross-attention itself is NOT written out here: it arrives as the cross_attention block — the
 * sequence cross-attention transformerBlock builds over the normalized activation and the encoder
 * context (the query projection, the context key/value projection on a branch, the query/key
 * normalization, the scores, the softmax and the output projection). Which projection adapter it
 * uses, and the context block it attends over, belong to the cross-attention build, not to this
 * residual wiring, and the language names neither as a value a stage can select, so the
 * cross-attention arrives as a block, exactly as the attention does in self_attention_sublayer.pdsl
 * and the feed-forward does in feed_forward_sublayer.pdsl.
 *
 * Data flow of one forward pass over a [batch, seq_len, dim] activation:
 *
 *   x                                                               [batch, seq_len, dim]
 *   accum {                            residual: x + sub-block(x)
 *     layernorm | rmsnorm              each position normalized over its dim features
 *                                                                   [batch, seq_len, dim]
 *     cross_attention                  the cross-attention sub-block over the encoder context
 *                                                                   [batch, seq_len, dim]
 *   }                                                               [batch, seq_len, dim]
 */

/** LayerNorm, then cross-attention, added back to the stream: x -> x + cross_attention(layernorm(x)). */
layer cross_attention_sublayer_layernorm(pre_norm_weight: weight, pre_norm_bias: weight,
                                         epsilon: float, cross_attention: block) {
    accum {
        layernorm(pre_norm_weight, pre_norm_bias, epsilon)
        cross_attention
    }
}

/** RMSNorm, then cross-attention, added back to the stream: x -> x + cross_attention(rmsnorm(x)). */
layer cross_attention_sublayer_rmsnorm(pre_norm_weight: weight, pre_norm_bias: weight,
                                       epsilon: float, cross_attention: block) {
    accum {
        rmsnorm(pre_norm_weight, pre_norm_bias, epsilon)
        cross_attention
    }
}
